COST ACCOUNTING (this replaces the old "cache = free" rule)

The 10 pre-downloaded rhea_aggregated files exist only because I fetched them manually; in deployment (an 11th, unseen case) every one of those points is a paid query. Therefore the ledger records TWO columns per query: served_from = {cache|api} and deployment_cost = 1 for every point the algorithm consumes (initial grid included). Pruning ratio and all reported query counts use deployment_cost, not api calls. New refinement queries in S3 go through query_rhea_aggregation.py (respect its rate/latency), are cached to OUT/cache/coverage.parquet keyed by (lat, lon), and are never repeated.

