THE 6 STEPS (run per case; start with the 2 cases I name)

S1 — Demand baseline

From RRC_data and throughput_volume: baseline = prior 3–4 weeks (bounded by available history), same hour-of-day + day-of-week, median + [P25, P75], aggregated over the outage window read from enodeb_neighbors_time/{target}.csv. Fit rho = PRB/volume from PRB/ + throughput_volume/ history (robust median ratio, NaN→0 first).


Figure: target RRC series + baseline band, outage window shaded.
Numbers: D_rrc [lo,hi], D_vol [lo,hi], rho, AND D_rrc_h2 [lo,hi] = the baseline RRC for the single hour that is outage_start + 2h (same weekday/hour matching). D_rrc_h2 exists because trend_residual (used in S5) is an hour-2 quantity — the conservation identity must compare like with like.
Decision: "Demand at risk ≈ {D_rrc} connections → non-trivial; next check neighbor capacity."


S2 — Neighbors and headroom

Neighbor list from enodeb_neighbors_time; distances from the decomposition summary CSV. Per-neighbor PRB baseline (same method as S1, NaN→0). headroom = 0.70 − PRB_baseline (floor 0); absorbable volume = Σ headroom/rho; SDR = absorbable/D_vol.


Figure: scatter distance vs headroom, point size = neighbor volume.
Number: SDR.
Decision: "SDR = {x} → capacity {is not | is} the binding constraint; capacity cannot tell us about coverage reach → run the spatial search."


S3 — Heuristic coverage search (core; budget B = 1200 deployment-cost queries)

Initial probes = ALL points in this case's rhea_aggregated JSON (*_aggregated.json) (their deployment cost is charged to the ledger). Label each probe: serving eNodeB ≠ target → unaffected; else by top1 backup RSRP: ≥ −105 dBm covered; [−110, −105) marginal; else hole. Cells = squares of 4 adjacent probes (3 km spacing initially). Uncertainty U = (spacing/3000) × min(1, 0.6·D + 0.4·M); D = normalized corner-label entropy + 0.5·[corner top1 backup eNodeBs differ], clipped to 1; M = exp(−|median corner RSRP − (−105)|/4). Priority = Pop × Area × U, Pop sampled from usa_pd_2019_1km.tif via the reader in build_cube_weights.py. Loop: heap-pop max cell → add 5 probes (edge midpoints + center; cache first, then real query via query_rhea_aggregation.py) → split into 4 half-spacing children → recompute → stop at budget / priority < 1e-3·initial max / spacing = 100 m.


Figure: adaptive probe map (probes colored by label, denser where refined, population underlay).
Numbers: deployment-cost queries used; pruning ratio vs exhaustive 100 m grid over the same extent; P_hole = population-weighted hole share.
Decision: "Boundary localized with {q} deployment-equivalent queries ({r}% of exhaustive); {P_hole}% of population in holes → convert map to demand routing."


S3b — Search validation against the 1 km reference

For every final leaf cell that overlaps points in rhea_aggregated_finer, compare the heuristic's label against labels computed from the 1 km data (same RSRP rules).


Figure: agreement map (agree / disagree cells).
Number: agreement rate, overall and within former boundary-band cells.
Decision: "Heuristic labels agree with the 1 km reference on {a}% of comparable cells → the budgeted search did not distort the qualitative picture."


S4 — Absorption prediction

Distribute D_rrc/D_vol over covered+marginal leaves by population weight; assign each leaf to its top1 backup eNodeB; per neighbor dPRB = rho × assigned volume (×1.4 for marginal leaves); demand beyond headroom → R_capacity; hole demand → R_hole; rest → R_absorbed.


Figure: stacked bar R_hole/R_capacity/R_absorbed + predicted per-neighbor shares.
Number: predicted interrupted = R_hole + R_capacity [lo,hi].
Decision: "Model predicts {lo}–{hi} interrupted, bottleneck {…} → confront with ground truth."


S5 — Conservation check using my ground-truth files (evaluated at outage hour 2)

Absorber set = rows with classification == "coincident_increase" in the coincident-increase CSV. Absorbed_h2 = Σ trend_residual over that set (sign convention per RESOLVED FACT 2: run the target-negative sanity check first). Conservation at matching granularity: Lost_rrc_h2 = D_rrc_h2 − Absorbed_h2. Then extrapolate to the whole window for the headline: absorbed_fraction = Absorbed_h2 / D_rrc_h2; Lost_rrc_window ≈ (1 − absorbed_fraction) × D_rrc — label it clearly as an hour-2-based extrapolation. Cross-check (mandatory — data confirmed available): recompute the absorber set and Absorbed with a P90-significance rule on the neighbors' raw RRC from kpi_{target}.csv over the full window (excluding hour 1) and report both.


Figure: waterfall in hour-2 terms — D_rrc_h2 minus each ground-truth absorber's trend_residual, remainder = Lost_h2.
Numbers: Lost_rrc_h2 [lo,hi]; Lost_rrc_window [lo,hi] (extrapolated); number of ground-truth absorbers; predicted-vs-actual overlap: how many of S4's top-3 predicted absorbers are in the coincident_increase set.
Decision: "Observed hour-2 loss {lo}–{hi} (window-extrapolated {lo}–{hi}) vs predicted {lo}–{hi}; {k}/3 of predicted top absorbers confirmed → {consistent | mismatch, note attribution}."


S6 — One-page conclusion card

Grade: A (no hole, no saturation, Lost≈0) / B (capacity-driven) / C (hole-driven) / D (both).


Figure: hole map + population overlay (reuse S3 final map, holes emphasized).
Numbers: grade + Lost interval.
Final sentence: "Case {id}: grade {G}. Estimated {lo}–{hi} connections interrupted, concentrated in {area}; bottleneck: {…}; {k}/3 predicted absorbers confirmed by ground truth; search validated at {a}% agreement vs 1 km reference."
